The Venn diagram shows counts of equally likely outcomes. The events $A$ and $B$ are independent.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1mm,y=1mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (76,48);
\draw (29,25) circle (18);
\draw (47,25) circle (18);
\path (20,35) node {$A$} (56,35) node {$B$};
\path (20,23) node {$8$} (38,23) node {$4$} (56,23) node {$6$} (68,7) node {$x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find $x$ using:
(a) $P(A)\times P(B)=P(A\cap B)$;
(b) $P(A\mid B)=P(A)$.
